# Overview
#
# Each phrase inflates a count without giving it (`a wide range of
# styles`), so the reader learns neither the items nor their number. The
# fix names the items or writes `many` or `several` (`the serif, sans,
# and mono styles`). The fix does not give the count, because a count of
# a set that can grow goes stale. The rule sits at Recommended, because
# `a variety of` also names a kind or means `different`.
#
# Expression
#
# `a host of` skips a following determiner (a word that introduces a
# noun, such as `the`, `a`, or `this`). `a significant number of` and
# its kin with `huge`, `substantial`, `considerable`, or `good` report
# here.
#
# False Positives
#
# `a host of` before a determiner names a machine (`a host of the
# cluster`). `a certain number of` and `a limited number of` stay out,
# because `many` changes or reverses their meaning. `a large amount of`
# stays out, because `many` does not fit a noun with no plural
# (`memory`).
#
# Related Rules
#
# `a large number of` stays out, because the Required ProseWordy reports
# it. The Optional ProseQuantity holds `various`, which also means
# `different`.
#
# Measurement
#
# The rule hit 46 lines in the measure.py corpus, and 18 of 20 sampled
# hits stood for a count that the sentence did not give. The misfires
# used `variety` for a kind (`lifetimes: a variety of generics`) or for
# `different` (`values with a variety of types`).
expr main [(rich set), (wide range), (wide variety), (plethora of), (myriad of), (a myriad), (wide array), (vast array), (broad range), (diverse range), (a host of ![the, this, that, a, an, each, every, its, their]), (a whole host), (a slew of), countless, numerous, (a variety of), (a [huge, significant, substantial, considerable, good] number of)]
let message "Vague quantity. Name the items, or write `many` or `several`."
let description "Flags phrases such as `wide range` and `plethora of` that inflate a count without giving it."
let becomes ""
let kind "Style"
allows "The catalog holds forty styles."
allows "The range covers ports 1 through 1024."
allows "Drain a host of the cluster before the upgrade."
allows "The job retries five times."
